[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Say what a grammar-file boundary means

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-GRAMMAR-AS-BOUNDARY
TITLE: Say what a grammar-file boundary means
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Say what a grammar file IS: a collection of node types and semantics that
represents a bounded goal -- not a full bounded context, since grammars can
overlay each other. Decide what that boundary implies (what may cross it,
what a file may assume about another) before the split lands.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Verbatim: "grammar files represent a sorta boundary, collection of node
types and semantics. not full blown bounded contexts, as they can overlay,
but alone they represent some kinda bounded goal." Filed as its own item
because the boundary semantics gate both the split and inheritance; if it is
only prose for the split node, collapse it at grooming.
<<<
